# Private paper route

## 1. Scientific objective and author claim

The paper uses compound 4b, (E)-5-(3,4-dimethylthiazol-2(3H)-ylidene)-3-ethyl-2-thioxothiazolidin-4-one, as the crystallographically characterized model for its computational interpretation. The author claim is that an optimized gas-phase DFT structure reproduces the experimentally determined molecular geometry sufficiently well to support interpretation of the spectroscopic and electronic-property results.

## 2. System and model boundary

Neutral, closed-shell 4b (C10H12N2OS3), one isolated molecule in the electronic ground state. The experimental comparison is to selected intramolecular XRD bond lengths, bond angles and torsion angles in SI Tables S1-S3; crystal packing is not optimized. The paper reports monoclinic P21 crystallization and E geometry of the inter-ring C=C bond.

## 3. Authors' implemented computational route

| Step | Purpose | Input | Method/software | Key parameters | Output | Source evidence |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Obtain equilibrium structure | Crystal structure of 4b | DFT geometry optimization; Gaussian 09/GaussView | B3LYP/6-311+G(d,p), ground state, gas phase, neutral singlet | Minimized molecular geometry | ev_doc_ca374b59f1ae_000067_74195f4aa69f; ev_doc_ca374b59f1ae_000398_9737daa0de07 |
| 2 | Verify stationary point | Optimized geometry | Harmonic frequency calculation in Gaussian 09 | Same B3LYP/6-311+G(d,p) model | Frequencies and IR intensities; real minimum check | ev_doc_ca374b59f1ae_000384_0ec54e303463 |
| 3 | Test structural agreement | Optimized geometry and XRD geometry | Geometry extraction and correlation analysis | Compare selected SI Tables S1-S3 parameters | Bond/angle/torsion comparisons and regression correlations | ev_doc_7d9d8139af59_000211_fcf77b5c1715; ev_doc_ca374b59f1ae_000403_60a6b484ec20; ev_doc_ca374b59f1ae_000404_80c951aa599d |
| 4 | Use model for interpretation | Optimized structures | Frontier-orbital/descriptor and spectral calculations | Reported in Section 2.7; not required as the present benchmark endpoint | Supporting electronic/spectroscopic interpretation | ev_doc_ca374b59f1ae_000067_74195f4aa69f |

## 4. Validation and analysis protocol

The frequency calculation is used to establish that the optimized structure is a true minimum. Selected bond lengths, bond angles and torsions are compared directly with the XRD values. The authors describe the rings as nearly coplanar and the ethyl substituent as approximately perpendicular; they report close calculated/experimental agreement and regression R2 values of 0.9883 and 0.9961 for the plotted geometry sets.

## 5. Private reference results

SI Tables S1-S3 contain the hidden DFT values paired with XRD values. Examples include DFT C1-S3 1.657 Å, C7-O1 1.228 Å, and DFT angles S1-C1-S3 122.191° and C1-N2-C7 119.649°. The paper reports DFT C=S and C=O lengths of about 1.655 and 1.235 Å, ring torsions near 174.5-179.9° and ethyl-related torsions near 90°, plus no imaginary frequencies as the minimum criterion.

## 6. Limitations and interpretation boundaries

The comparison is between an isolated-molecule gas-phase equilibrium structure and a crystal structure, so packing, temperature and crystal disorder are not reproduced. Only the selected SI geometry observables are scored. Agreement with XRD does not by itself validate the full photophysical or antioxidant interpretation.
